# Vercel falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, which coupled two
# unrelated decisions: keeping the Williams build out of git also removed it
# from the deployment, and production 404'd on /williams. Deployment contents
# and repository contents are now stated separately.
.DS_Store
.vercel
node_modules
*.log
.env
.env.*
*_BM_*.csv
.fixtures/

# Internal-only, and until 2026-09-17 all three were served publicly at 200.
# Nothing the site renders fetches from any of them — every reference is a code
# comment naming a generator ("Source of truth is tools/webgl_guard.js") or
# provenance, never a runtime URL. Checked before excluding.
#
#   docs/      — TRACKING.md was 186 KB of internal tracker on the open web:
#                client names, decisions, and repeated mentions of the project
#                that must not appear publicly at all — the very thing that rule
#                exists to prevent. (This file is not deployed, but the REPO is
#                public, so naming that project here defeated the point too.)
#   tools/     — seed_demo_deck.mjs carries a hard-coded demo share token that
#                TRACKING.md itself called "one guess away". Revoked 2026-09-15.
#   supabase/  — schema, RLS policies and edge-function source.
#
# A static host serves whatever it is given, so "unreferenced" is not "private":
# a guessed URL still returns the file.
docs/
tools/
supabase/

# Not public yet (2026-09-18). The nav and footer links were removed too, but
# removing links is not hiding: this host serves whatever it is given, so the
# page has to leave the DEPLOYMENT or /studio/ still answers 200 to anyone who
# guesses it. Preview it locally instead:
#   python3 -m http.server 8899   ->   http://localhost:8899/studio/
# To publish: delete this line, restore the STUDIO nav/footer links on
# index.html, faq/ and privacy/, and redeploy.
studio/
